==English==

===Etymology===
1610s, from {{der|en|la|pītuītārius||mucous}}, from {{m|la|pītuīta||[[clammy]] [[moisture]], [[phlegm]], [[mucus]], [[slime]]}}, possibly from {{der|en|ine-pro|*peyH-||to be [[fat]], [[swell]]}}. Taken as the name for the gland because it was believed that it channeled mucus to the nose. As a noun by 1899.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/pɪˈtjuːɪt(ə)ɹi/|/pɪˈt͡ʃuːɪt(ə)ɹi/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/pɪˈtuɪˌtɛɹi/}}

